            <ArticleTitle>Acquired internal mammary artery to pulmonary artery fistula following bypass surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>280-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two patients with acquired fistulas between the internal mammary and pulmonary arteries after coronary bypass surgery. This is a rare complication of bypass surgery and may be a cause of recurrent angina postoperatively due to coronary artery steal. A table of all the cases reported in the literature is compiled.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
